# C-Style Block Comment Checker ($\varepsilon$-NFA)

This project implements an **$\varepsilon$-NFA (Non-Deterministic Finite Automaton with $\varepsilon$-transitions)** that parses and validates C-style block comments (`/* ... */`).

---

## 1. Visual Automaton Diagram

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> q0
    q0 --> q1 : /
    q1 --> q2 : *
    q2 --> q3 : ε
    q3 --> q2 : a, /
    q2 --> q4 : *
    q4 --> q4 : *
    q4 --> q2 : a
    q4 --> q5 : /
    q5 --> [*]
```

---

## 2. Formal Definition

The $\varepsilon$-NFA is formally defined by the tuple $M = (Q, \Sigma, \delta, q_0, F)$:

* **States ($Q$):** $\{q_0, q_1, q_2, q_3, q_4, q_5\}$
* **Alphabet ($\Sigma$):** $\{/, *, a\}$ *(where $a$ represents any character other than $/$ or $*$)*
* **Start State ($q_0$):** $q_0$
* **Accept State ($F$):** $\{q_5\}$
* **Language ($L$):** Set of all valid C-style block comments starting with `/*` and ending with `*/`.

### Transition Table

| State | $\varepsilon$ | `/` | `*` | `a` |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **$\to q_0$** | $\emptyset$ | $\{q_1\}$ | $\emptyset$ | $\emptyset$ |
| **$q_1$** | $\emptyset$ | $\emptyset$ | $\{q_2\}$ | $\emptyset$ |
| **$q_2$** | $\{q_3\}$ | $\emptyset$ | $\{q_4\}$ | $\emptyset$ |
| **$q_3$** | $\emptyset$ | $\{q_2\}$ | $\emptyset$ | $\{q_2\}$ |
| **$q_4$** | $\emptyset$ | $\{q_5\}$ | $\{q_4\}$ | $\{q_2\}$ |
| **$*q_5$** | $\emptyset$ | $\emptyset$ | $\emptyset$ | $\emptyset$ |

